      is by ``repr`` of the canonical pair, which exists for every canonical
      form (canonical values contain no sets), so dict key order never
      affects the result and two equal dicts always canonicalize equally.
    - list  -> (tag, tuple of canonical items), order preserved.
    - tuple -> (tag, tuple of canonical items).
    - set / frozenset -> (tag, sorted tuple of canonical items), since
      sets compare equal regardless of order.
    - anything else (scalars, bytes, user objects) -> (type, value), which
      is hashable for everything that is hashable at all; a TypeError
      propagates to the caller for the pathological case.
